      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Four observed cells produce a double difference:\n  D_{ii';jk} = m_ij - m_ik - m_i'j + m_i'k.\n\nAdditive terms cancel. Under rank one:\n  D_{ii';jk} = (u_i - u_i') (v_j - v_k).\n\nIdentification logic:\n  1. Rectangles identify relative interaction contrasts.\n  2. Anchors fix gauge/normalization.\n  3. Overlapping rectangles propagate worker and firm factor information.\n  4. Target functionals may be identified before the entire schedule is point-identified.\n\nThis is the bipartite analogue of cycle logic, but it is not the same graph as firm-mover cycles.",
